WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.037
This is Centaur.

2
00:00:02.748 --> 00:00:05.570
Let's see what happens when a prospect emails you,

3
00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:08.787
and how Centaur's AI writes a reply that's ready to send.

4
00:00:09.716 --> 00:00:13.154
Marcus, at Northfield Logistics, has just replied to Cody.

5
00:00:13.849 --> 00:00:16.068
He's interested, but he has three questions.

6
00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.964
Will Centaur work for a team of twenty five?

7
00:00:19.748 --> 00:00:22.503
How does it compare with Salesforce, which they use today?

8
00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:25.059
And can he see it running this month?

9
00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:28.140
Moments later, a draft is waiting.

10
00:00:28.955 --> 00:00:32.143
It answers all three questions, clearly and in order.

11
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.449
It explains the pricing for twenty five users.

12
00:00:36.125 --> 00:00:40.034
It handles the Salesforce question using the points from your approved battle card.

13
00:00:41.099 --> 00:00:44.049
And it offers three times when Cody is actually free,

14
00:00:44.049 --> 00:00:46.331
taken straight from his Outlook calendar.

15
00:00:47.324 --> 00:00:48.778
So where does all this come from?

16
00:00:49.543 --> 00:00:50.613
Not from the internet.

17
00:00:51.402 --> 00:00:51.958
From you.

18
00:00:52.961 --> 00:00:54.301
First, AI Training.

19
00:00:55.085 --> 00:00:59.883
This is where you teach Centaur about your business: what you sell, who you sell to,

20
00:00:59.883 --> 00:01:02.338
your pricing, and what makes you different.

21
00:01:03.494 --> 00:01:05.865
The agent reads it before every reply it writes.

22
00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:08.339
Next, your battle cards.

23
00:01:08.886 --> 00:01:11.137
Each one is researched, with its sources,

24
00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.882
and the agent only uses the cards you've approved.

25
00:01:14.768 --> 00:01:18.392
If there's no approved card, it says nothing about the competitor at all.

26
00:01:19.373 --> 00:01:20.859
It knows the conversation, too.

27
00:01:21.475 --> 00:01:24.967
Every email, call note and Teams meeting summary on the record,

28
00:01:24.967 --> 00:01:28.126
so it never asks a question that's already been answered.

29
00:01:29.162 --> 00:01:30.670
It follows your sales method.

30
00:01:31.388 --> 00:01:34.449
With BANT, it quietly works out budget, authority,

31
00:01:34.449 --> 00:01:36.959
need and timing as the conversation goes.

32
00:01:38.091 --> 00:01:39.186
And it writes like you.

33
00:01:39.622 --> 00:01:43.736
It learns your tone from your own example emails, and signs off the way you do.

34
00:01:44.972 --> 00:01:46.241
There are firm rules, too.

35
00:01:46.657 --> 00:01:48.206
It never invents a meeting time,

36
00:01:48.206 --> 00:01:51.933
and it never makes claims about a competitor that aren't on an approved card.

37
00:01:53.349 --> 00:01:54.893
Now the draft waits for Cody.

38
00:01:55.762 --> 00:01:58.765
He reads it, changes a word if he wants to, and sends it.

39
00:01:59.394 --> 00:02:01.553
Thirty seconds, instead of thirty minutes.

40
00:02:02.773 --> 00:02:04.052
Centaur CRM.

41
00:02:04.632 --> 00:02:07.256
Replies that sound like your best rep, in moments.

42
00:02:08.043 --> 00:02:11.587
Book a demonstration today, at centaurcrm.com.

